<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  UI text, in ENGLISH (the default). The Portuguese translation lives in
  res/values-pt/strings.xml and the head unit picks it by its locale.

  The rule: no text that appears on screen may go back to being a literal in the
  middle of the Java. Displayed language is a resource choice, not a code edit.

  Concatenation becomes a PLACEHOLDER, never a fragment. "Enviando (a cada " + n
  + "s)" cannot be translated: word order moves between languages and a dangling
  piece carries no context. Hence %1$d, %1$s and friends.

  Values wrapped in "quotes" have leading/trailing or repeated spaces that aapt2
  would otherwise collapse. The AC readout depends on exactly three spaces around
  its separators.

  NOT here: MQTT topics, SharedPreferences keys, log messages, theme ids, and the
  Home Assistant entity names in Telemetry.java (renaming those would rename the
  user's HA entities and break their automations).

  This file is the SOURCE. It was once merged from per-file fragments by a
  scratchpad script that no longer exists — edit it directly.
-->
